&lt;div class="tag country"&gt;Countries: South Sudan, Democratic Republic of the Congo&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;div class="tag source"&gt;Source: International Organization for Migration&lt;/div&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://reliefweb.int/sites/default/files/styles/thumbnail/public/previews/1b/13/1b13fb43-d3fe-54f5-919b-bdc4b816d112.png" alt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;Please refer to the attached Infographic.&lt;/p&gt;
 &lt;p&gt;South Sudan (SSD) shares its southern borders with the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), Uganda and Kenya, with continuous, high-volume movement that remains largely undocumented at community level. Ebola transmission continues in the DRC following the outbreak in May 2026, and Kenya confirmed cases in Nairobi in October linked to travel from the DRC through Uganda. To inform preparedness along these routes, the third round of the Flow Monitoring Survey includes an Ebola Virus Disease (EVD) module examining travellers’ awareness, knowledge of where to report suspected cases and intended sources of care if they became ill.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Findings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Entries exceeded exits at six of the eight flow monitoring points (FMPs). Movement was concentrated at a few points. Nimule Border alone recorded 54 per cent of all counted movements; together with Juba International Airport and Jale it accounted for 85 per cent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The route network centred on Juba, which was the destination for 68 per cent of inflow respondents and the departure county for 73 per cent of outflow respondents&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Along the route to DRC, nearly all respondents had reported awareness of Ebola (99%), had received prevention information in the previous month (97%) and knew where to report a suspected case (98%), with health centres reported most commonly as the most trusted sources of information (70%)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-border movement connected the monitored points with areas affected by Ebola. Along the DRC route, 96 per cent of inflow respondents had departed from Dungu and 97 per cent of outflow respondents were heading there, following the reported expansion of the outbreak to Dungu health zone.&lt;/p&gt;

